      "title": "Mail Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Closing Date: 07/12/2026 Department: USM Mailroom Category: Mail Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Gorham, ME, United States The University of Southern Maine is committed to building a culturally diverse team of leaders, faculty, and staff. Multilingual applicants would be an asset to this role. Women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans are encouraged to apply. If you are a supervisor or leader with experience in mail services and delivery and/or possess strong administrative or leadership skills, then check out this opportunity! The University of Southern Maine is seeking applicants for Mail Services Supervisor within our Facilities Management team. Directly supervising a small team and overseeing all things related to mail services, this position is primarily assigned to our Gorham Campus and is responsible for the day-to-day operation of mail services on both our Gorham and Portland campuses. Pay and Benefits This is a full-time regular on campus position that is core to USM’s ability to deliver an exceptional and affordable educational experience to students in Maine and across the country; AND an opportunity for you to advance your education with our tuition waiver program! This position will pay $21.93/hour. The primary work schedule of Monday through Friday, 8:00AM – 4:30PM with some evenings and weekends as necessary. The University of Southern Maine offers highly competitive benefits for full-time and eligible part-time employees that includes (but is not limited to): 13 paid holidays plus earned vacation time and sick time. Health, dental and vision insurance. Short-term and long-term disability insurance. Basic life insurance and supplemental life insurance. A tuition waiver program for employees and their spouse or dependent child(ren). A 403(b)-retirement plan. Free access to the METRO system, including the Husky Line with service between our Portland and Gorham campuses. About the University The